    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, I completely support what Aaron Rodgers has done. He is, and I appreciate his courage in defending his own personal health economy, defending his freedom. You know, it's not surprising but still shocking that all the attacks he's having to endure, you know, endure now because of him just standing up for his own personal choice. I mean, whatever happened to my body, my choice. I guess that only applies to abortion, apparently. But, you know, I completely support him. These mandates are pointless. I held an event last week in Washington, D.C., where we had the vaccine injured. And by the way, vaccine injuries are real. They're only rare and mild if they don't happen to you. If they happen to you, they can be quite severe and serious. We showed that. Plus, we also had experts. Well, one of the experts had a very simple decision tree, had two boxes. One box said, are the COVID-19 vaccines effective? And if you follow the S line down, it went to the second box and said, well, then the vaccine mandates are pointless. Right? If they're effective, what do you care whether somebody next to you as a vaccinated or unvaccinated? Unfortunately, guys, we're on the we're following the no line now because these vaccines, unfortunately, are not as effective and safe as we all hope, but it goes to the exact same decision line and the mandates are pointless. I mean, if you can get infected, if you can spread COVID, if you can get seriously on die from COVID, what's the point in mandating them? And I think that's the exact same point that Aaron Rodgers was making. It's insane. to force this on anybody, and guys, it's really insane to force this on children. Five to 11-year-olds, they have virtually no risk of serious complications from COVID unless they have other comorbidities. They do run a risk of myocarditis. There is no medical necessity for children, and yet our CDC FDA, the COVID gods, as I call them, present Biden, they're pushing these vaccines on children. I mean, that's a travesty.",
